<BaseLayout title="Medical Review Policy" description="How RPT Clinic reviews educational health-library content."><div class="container reading-width section prose"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Medical Review Policy' }]} /><h1>Medical Review Policy</h1><p>Health-library content is created for general education. Before publication, assign each article to a qualified reviewer and record the reviewer name, credentials and review date in its frontmatter.</p><h2>Editorial safeguards</h2><ul><li>Use plain language and state what the article covers.</li><li>Review content for accuracy, clarity and appropriate clinical context.</li><li>Update material when clinical guidance, services or local practice changes.</li><li>Avoid diagnosing readers or making outcome guarantees.</li><li>Include an appropriate emergency and medical-advice disclaimer.</li></ul><p>This starter policy must be reviewed and customized by the clinic's leadership, legal counsel and clinical team before launch.</p></div></BaseLayout>
